# System Architecture
The system follows a client-server architecture:

#Frontend
- Handles UI rendering.
- Sends requests to backend APIs.
- Displays products, carts and user actions.

#Backend
- Processes the requests from frontend.
- Handles cart operations and authentication.
- Communicates with the database.

# Database
-Stores the users, products, carts and orders.
- Ensures persistent data storage.

#Frontend Implementation
The frontend was developed using:
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- React.js

Responsibilities include:
- Rendering homepage and product page.
- Handling user interactions like login, register, cart actions, etc.
- Managing navigation between pages and components.
- Communicating with backend using API requests.

 Key Frontend Features
   Landing Page/Homepage:
  - Displays featured or all available products
  - Provides navigation to login, register, and cart
  - Acts as the entry point of the application

    Product Listing Page:
   - Dynamically displays products fetched from backend.
   - Each product includes the name, price, image and "add to cart button"
   - Supports user interaction for selecting items

     Authentication Page:
   Login Page
    - Accepts user credentials (email/password)
    - Sends login request to backend
    - Stores authentication session on success
   Registration Page
    - Collects user details
    - Sends registration request to backend
    - Redirects user after successful account creation

     Shopping Cart Page:
    - Displays all selected products
    - Shows quantity and total price calculation
    - Allows to:
      Increase/decrease quantity
      Remove items
      Update dynamically when cart changes

     Checkout Page:
     - Displays final order summary
    - Confirms purchase action
    - Sends order data to backend
    - Clears cart after successful order

     Navigation System
     - Allows movement between pages without breaking application flow
     - Maintains user session across pages
 
    Frontend Logic Flow
 Application Load Flow:
 - User opens the application
 - Frontend initializes application state
 - API request is sent to backend to fetch products
 - Backend returns product data
 - Frontend renders products dynamically on homepage
 Product Interaction Flow:
 - User views product list
 - User clicks “Add to Cart”
 - Frontend sends product ID to backend via API
 - Backend updates cart in database
 - Backend sends success response
 - Frontend updates cart UI immediately
 Authentication Flow:
 - User enters login credentials
 - Frontend validates input format (basic validation)
 - Credentials sent to backend API
 - Backend checks user database
  If valid:
  - authentication token/session is generated
  - user is redirected to homepage/dashboard
   If invalid:
  - error message displayed on UI
 Cart Management Flow:
 - User adds product to cart
 - Frontend updates cart state temporarily
 - Backend stores cart update permanently
 - Frontend syncs with backend response
 - Cart page reflects updated items and total price
 Checkout Flow:
 - User navigates to checkout page
 - Frontend retrieves cart data
 - Total price is calculated
 - User confirms order
 - Frontend sends order request to backend
 - Backend creates order record
 - Cart is cleared after successful transaction
 - Confirmation message is displayed
 State Mangement Flow:
The frontend maintains application state such as:
 - Logged-in user state
 - Cart contents
 - Product list
 - Loading states
State updates occur when:
 - API responses are received
 - User performs actions (add/remove cart items)
 - Authentication status changes

Frontend-Backend Communication Model
The frontend communicates with the backend using REST API calls.
Process:
 - Frontend sends HTTP request (GET/POST/DELETE)
 - Backend processes request
 - Backend sends JSON response
 - Frontend updates UI based on response

